# Task 044 (user-approved option A, 2026-08-21): Gradle-native R8 adapter.
#
# The suppressed descriptors below are CLASS-retained annotations referenced by
# generated aconfig flag JARs (e.g. com.android.wifi.flags.FeatureFlags). They
# are build/optimizer-only signatures with no APK runtime behavior: not
# instantiated, reflected, or JNI-resolved on any supported runtime path
# (classified in Task 043).
#
# This file deliberately does NOT supply the annotation class (no JAR/AAR,
# no SysUISdk mutation) and does NOT import any part of AOSP's
# aconfig_proguard.flags: no keep/assumevalues/assumenosideeffects rules and
# no aconfig flag folding are introduced, so flag runtime semantics stay
# unchanged. The exact-FQN suppressions below only tell R8 that the unresolved
# annotation references may be ignored.
#
# Second same-family instance (task 060, user-approved option A, 2026-08-25):
# -dontwarn com.android.aconfig.annotations.AssumeFalseForR8 — the false-valued
# sibling of AssumeTrueForR8 from the same aconfig pipeline. It entered the
# classpath via the task 055 window-flags jar (libs/systemui-aconfig-flags.jar,
# com.android.window.flags.FeatureFlags, RuntimeInvisibleAnnotations / CLASS
# retention) and is never runtime-resolved.
# Third instance (task 060, user-approved option A, 2026-08-25):
# -dontobfuscate — aligns R8 obfuscation semantics with the AOSP Soong build.
# Evidence: Soong appends -dontobfuscate when the bp `optimize.obfuscate` prop is
# unset (build/soong/java/dex.go:545); SystemUI's Android.bp never sets
# obfuscate:true (SystemUI_optimized_defaults sets optimize/shrink/
# shrink_resources only) → AOSP SystemUI is NEVER obfuscated. AGP's
# isMinifyEnabled obfuscates by default → getClass().getSimpleName()-keyed
# DumpManager registrations collided (39 classes renamed to simple name "a",
# incl. multiple dumpable registrants) → 1290 FATAL 'a' is already registered
# crash-loop on device (task 060, 2026-08-26).
#
# Wired only into the minified `release` build type of app/build.gradle.kts.
-dontwarn com.android.aconfig.annotations.AssumeTrueForR8
-dontwarn com.android.aconfig.annotations.AssumeFalseForR8
-dontobfuscate
#
# Fourth instance (task 061, user-approved 2026-08-26): keep rules blocking R8
# horizontal class merging. R8 full-mode merging collapsed the identity-distinct
# CoreStartables (CoreStartable$Nop singleton, NoOpCoreStartable fresh instance,
# FeatureFlagsReleaseStartable fresh instance) into one runtime class; DumpManager
# registers dumpables by class name (module::class.java.name) and rejects distinct
# instances sharing a name → IllegalArgumentException 'CoreStartable$Nop is already
# registered' → 195-FATAL crash loop (task 060b round-3 crash). -keep (not merely
# -keepnames) is required: renaming is already off via -dontobfuscate; only -keep
# prevents the merge itself.
-keep class com.android.systemui.CoreStartable$Nop { *; }
-keep class com.android.systemui.NoOpCoreStartable { *; }
-keep class com.android.systemui.flags.FeatureFlagsReleaseStartable { *; }
